## 8. Phase 1 checklist

<!--
Tick every box before declaring Phase 1 done and moving to Phase 2.
-->

### Evidence gate

- [ ] `## Evidence` section filled with overall status + verification commands
- [ ] Every `file:line` reference in body tagged `[verified]` or `[estimated]`
- [ ] >=50% of references are `[verified]` (otherwise escalate for re-dissect)
- [ ] No purely invented paths (catch with `find /path/to/repo -name <claimed-file>`)

### Metadata

- [ ] Target URL/source captured and verified reachable
- [ ] Target type classified (source / binary / mobile / firmware / protocol)
- [ ] Classification assigned (app / library / framework / service / ...)
- [ ] Version pinned (tag or commit SHA recorded)
- [ ] License identified and compatibility checked
- [ ] Reusability goal declared (port / integrate / reference / audit)

### Recon

- [ ] `tree -L 2` captured
- [ ] `cloc` (or equivalent) run, totals recorded
- [ ] Direct deps counted, lockfile inspected
- [ ] Biggest file identified
- [ ] Test coverage sanity-checked

### Risk

- [ ] Auth model classified
- [ ] Crypto library identified
- [ ] Input validation strategy classified
- [ ] Secret scan run (gitleaks / trufflehog / similar)
- [ ] CVE scan run (trivy / grype / snyk / similar)
- [ ] License compatibility checked

### Planning

- [ ] 3-7 deep-dive candidates selected with rationale
- [ ] Priorities assigned (P0..P3)
- [ ] IN/OUT of scope documented
- [ ] Open questions list created
- [ ] Companion runs decided (neodoo-integrate yes/no)

### Hand-off

- [ ] File committed to `dissects/<system>/triagem.md`
- [ ] Cross-links added to `wiki/index.md` once Phase 3 starts
- [ ] Stakeholder notified of scope and timeline estimate